  "description": {
    "format": "nuke_help_html",
    "plain_text": "Outputs a shader material that projects the input image through the input camera onto the 3D object. Use 3D/shader/apply to put the output of this operator onto a 3D object. Note: Input image source must be a texture input (a 2D node) and not another shader. To combine multiple projections together use the MergeMat/MergeSurface node. Enable the raycasting feature on the ScanlineRender node to enable occlusion testing.",
    "source": "nuke.Node.help()",
    "text": "Outputs a shader material that projects the input image through the input camera onto the 3D object. Use 3D/shader/apply to put the output of this operator onto a 3D object.\n\nNote: Input image source must be a texture input (a 2D node) and not another shader. To combine multiple projections together use the MergeMat/MergeSurface node.\n\nEnable the raycasting feature on the ScanlineRender node to enable occlusion testing. "
  },
